WEBVTT

00:07.901 --> 00:13.661
Let's laugh and cry.
chanto waraimasho, nakimasho

00:14.161 --> 00:19.751
We need to fill up our hearts.
kokoro no nakami wo juujitsu sasenakuccha
Subs originally by Froth-Bite
Manually retyped by #Retrofit@IRC.Rizon.Net
Raws by Darkside-Raws

00:19.791 --> 00:28.341
Making matching memories with you...
anata to osoroi no omoide tsukuruno ga

00:28.341 --> 00:30.211
...is important.
daiji daiji

00:31.591 --> 00:34.141
Sometimes I become...
sunao ni narenakattari

00:34.471 --> 00:37.971
...almost dishonest and mean
ijiwaru shichaisouna hi aruno

00:39.471 --> 00:40.811
That's because...
sore wa...

00:42.811 --> 00:45.561
I love you and adore you,
daisuki de taisetsu de

00:45.691 --> 00:48.901
and I don't want to be apart from you.
hanaretaku nai sei nano nante

00:50.861 --> 00:51.861
That's the truth.
henne

00:54.411 --> 01:01.121
I just want to cuddle...
hontou wa itsumo nuku nuku shitetai

01:01.451 --> 01:03.461
...with you.
futaride

01:04.461 --> 01:10.171
So let's laugh and cry.
dakara waraimashou, nakimashou

01:10.841 --> 01:16.261
We need to keep our hearts warm.
kokoro no ondo wo atatame awanakucha

01:16.471 --> 01:24.771
The fate that made us meet...
anata to deaeta unmei ho subetega

01:24.771 --> 01:26.601
...is important.
daiji daiji

01:30.971 --> 01:35.391
Four princesses lived happily in a castle.

01:35.391 --> 01:39.101
They looked happy as they ate their favorite umeboshi.

01:39.941 --> 01:42.151
Sour!

01:42.151 --> 01:44.901
One day, they had a problem.

01:46.281 --> 01:49.151
There was only one umeboshi left.

01:49.151 --> 01:51.611
What shall we do?

01:51.611 --> 01:52.571
Oh, yes!

01:55.161 --> 01:55.201
Magic Curtain

01:55.201 --> 01:57.291
The magic curtain!
Magic Curtain

01:57.291 --> 01:58.661
Magic Curtain

01:59.001 --> 02:01.831
Cover a chair with the magic curtain, then...

02:01.831 --> 02:04.631
Chi-chin pui pui!

02:04.631 --> 02:05.921
Go!

02:06.211 --> 02:07.501
How mysterious!

02:07.501 --> 02:09.971
Now there are two chairs!

02:09.971 --> 02:12.881
Now, let's multiply the umeboshi!

02:12.881 --> 02:15.261
Chi-chin pui pui!

02:15.261 --> 02:16.681
Go!

02:16.681 --> 02:18.021
It was successful!

02:18.021 --> 02:20.351
Now there is another pot of umeboshi!

02:21.231 --> 02:23.941
Yay! Successful!

02:24.651 --> 02:25.941
Oh?

02:25.941 --> 02:30.651
The magic curtain gave them an extra princess along with the extra pot of umeboshi.

02:31.491 --> 02:35.031
Now, with their umeboshi, the five princesses are going...

02:35.031 --> 02:38.581
Mmmmm, sour!

02:39.291 --> 02:43.501
<b>...maybe</b>

02:44.041 --> 02:44.881
Storage

02:44.881 --> 02:46.731
Um...
Storage

02:46.731 --> 02:46.791
Um...

02:51.171 --> 02:54.511
Looks like Kozue-chan transformed again.

02:58.261 --> 02:58.891
Um...

03:01.931 --> 03:05.311
But she's a type I haven't seen before.

03:05.311 --> 03:08.361
You've done it again, Shiratori-san.

03:09.021 --> 03:11.151
And it's Her this time.

03:11.151 --> 03:13.031
This will be tough.

03:13.031 --> 03:13.991
Her?

03:14.361 --> 03:17.161
Nobody knows her name.

03:17.161 --> 03:22.291
Because nobody has heard her speak.

03:22.911 --> 03:26.711
We've tried really hard to get close to her before,

03:27.171 --> 03:29.751
but we couldn't even get her name.

03:29.751 --> 03:31.091
I see.

03:32.551 --> 03:33.721
Um...

03:33.721 --> 03:34.761
Hello?

03:34.841 --> 03:36.471
Hello?

03:39.431 --> 03:41.311
She's not coming out...

03:46.901 --> 03:48.981
We want to talk to you a little.

03:48.981 --> 03:50.151
Can we?

03:56.491 --> 03:57.741
Um...

04:00.581 --> 04:03.081
That's how it goes every time.

04:03.501 --> 04:04.871
I see.

04:04.871 --> 04:07.081
But I'm a little relieved.

04:07.081 --> 04:11.001
She might be shy, but she looks like she's harmless.

04:11.001 --> 04:13.591
But still...

04:13.921 --> 04:17.511
How can we leave the situation like this?!

04:17.511 --> 04:20.221
Shiratori-san, you cold-hearted, ignorant fool!

04:20.221 --> 04:21.641
No, I didn't mean...

04:21.641 --> 04:22.511
Fine!

04:22.971 --> 04:26.141
I'll call Momo-san and the others here!

04:26.731 --> 04:29.061
Call?

04:30.361 --> 04:33.321
Everyone!

04:33.321 --> 04:36.361
She showed up!

04:36.361 --> 04:37.071
What?!

04:37.451 --> 04:38.661
She did?!

04:38.661 --> 04:39.661
Swe didth?!

04:39.861 --> 04:42.491
Are you sure about that?!

04:43.201 --> 04:45.081
Are you sure it's Her?

04:45.081 --> 04:46.291
Where? Where?

04:46.291 --> 04:48.211
Are you absolutely sure?

04:48.581 --> 04:50.001
It's Her!

04:56.381 --> 04:58.471
Dear Narutakisou Residents,

04:58.761 --> 05:03.681
according to Information Officer Tamami, She has shown up again.

05:05.181 --> 05:07.641
This is our chance to break the ice.

05:07.641 --> 05:12.941
Do your best, get her attention, and open her heart.

05:12.941 --> 05:13.731
Over!

05:14.981 --> 05:18.361
Why are they so excited?

05:18.361 --> 05:19.111
HEY!

05:19.571 --> 05:21.611
Why aren't you responding, Lieutenant Shiratori?!

05:21.611 --> 05:23.201
Be more gutsy!

05:23.201 --> 05:24.871
Gutsy?

05:24.871 --> 05:28.661
I was just thinking you're more energetic than usual.

05:29.001 --> 05:31.001
WHAT?!

05:31.001 --> 05:35.001
Don't you understand our feelings of loneliness?!

05:35.001 --> 05:36.211
Isn't that a little exaggerated?
Don't you understand our feelings of loneliness?!

05:36.211 --> 05:37.171
Isn't that a little exaggerated?

05:44.971 --> 05:47.811
Why does she avoid us?

05:47.811 --> 05:50.521
We want to talk with her.

05:50.521 --> 05:54.771
She does seem to have some interest in us.

05:54.771 --> 05:57.481
But why does she hide every time?

05:57.481 --> 05:58.781
So sad.

05:59.191 --> 06:00.241
I see.

06:00.241 --> 06:01.611
I understand.

06:01.611 --> 06:03.911
I'll give my modest support too.

06:03.911 --> 06:05.531
Shiratori-kun!

06:05.531 --> 06:08.121
I knew you would understand!

06:08.121 --> 06:10.791
That's how residents of Narutakisou are supposed to be!

06:10.791 --> 06:14.291
Okay, so would you please wipe your nose?

06:14.291 --> 06:17.461
It was totally bad the last time.

06:17.461 --> 06:20.421
But we still can't give up.

06:20.421 --> 06:21.801
No, we can't.

06:28.221 --> 06:30.561
Now that we have agreed on our objectives,

06:30.561 --> 06:33.561
initiate Project Open Her Shy Heart!

06:35.021 --> 06:35.401
Momono Megumi's Challenge!

06:35.401 --> 06:38.441
Watch how I tackle this challenge!
Momono Megumi's Challenge!

06:38.441 --> 06:38.501
Momono Megumi's Challenge!

06:39.151 --> 06:40.241
Hey, long time no see!

06:40.241 --> 06:41.281
How have you been?

06:41.281 --> 06:43.741
I'm doing really great!

06:45.701 --> 06:47.871
By the way, what are you reading?

06:47.871 --> 06:50.501
That looks like a difficult book.

06:50.501 --> 06:52.581
You were reading something the other day too, weren't you?

06:52.581 --> 06:53.921
You love to read?

06:59.131 --> 06:59.381
The Real Thing Starts Now!!

06:59.381 --> 07:01.801
The Real Thing starts now!
The Real Thing Starts Now!!

07:01.801 --> 07:01.811
The Real Thing Starts Now!!

07:02.341 --> 07:03.221
Hey.

07:04.301 --> 07:05.301
Hey.

07:06.391 --> 07:07.141
Hey.

07:08.761 --> 07:10.061
Looking down...

07:11.221 --> 07:13.101
Hey!

07:14.601 --> 07:15.731
So fruitless...

07:16.651 --> 07:17.771
Sayoko's Challenge!

07:17.771 --> 07:21.321
I've been thinking that we're on the same wavelength.
Sayoko's Challenge!

07:21.321 --> 07:21.501
Sayoko's Challenge!

07:21.861 --> 07:25.031
They sure have similar auras.

07:25.031 --> 07:26.451
We can expect a lot.

07:36.621 --> 07:38.171
It didn't work.

07:38.171 --> 07:39.921
You didn't do anything.

07:40.061 --> 07:40.801
Asami's Challenge!

07:40.801 --> 07:41.671
Hello.
Asami's Challenge!

07:41.671 --> 07:42.881
Asami's Challenge!
I'm Kurosaki Asami.

07:42.881 --> 07:43.881
Asami's Challenge!
Do you remember me?

07:43.881 --> 07:44.091
Asami's Challenge!

07:44.341 --> 07:46.341
I'll show you my best gag!

07:46.341 --> 07:47.221
Watch!

07:49.471 --> 07:50.101
Cat!

07:50.101 --> 07:50.971
Meow.

07:51.061 --> 07:51.891
Meow.

07:51.971 --> 07:53.521
Meow.

07:54.931 --> 07:56.561
That was great, Asami.

07:56.561 --> 07:58.191
My stomach hurts.

07:58.191 --> 07:59.521
Wasn't it?

07:59.521 --> 08:01.321
A-Asami-chan...

08:01.481 --> 08:01.861
Tamami and Johnny (Haibara)'s Challenge!

08:01.861 --> 08:05.821
Well, well, it's finally our turn.
Tamami and Johnny (Haibara)'s Challenge!

08:05.821 --> 08:06.321
Tamami and Johnny (Haibara)'s Challenge!

08:06.321 --> 08:09.201
Nobody can refuse us, the best team!
Tamami and Johnny (Haibara)'s Challenge!

08:09.201 --> 08:09.381
Tamami and Johnny (Haibara)'s Challenge!

08:10.661 --> 08:12.791
I'm home.

08:12.791 --> 08:16.121
Where have you been so late?!

08:16.121 --> 08:16.961
Shut up!

08:16.961 --> 08:18.081
Oh!

08:18.081 --> 08:21.131
Don't question what I do!

08:21.131 --> 08:22.751
What?!

08:22.751 --> 08:26.591
You old, heartless, useless...!

08:28.051 --> 08:32.351
Who do you think is feeding you?!

08:32.971 --> 08:35.521
Somebody!

08:42.231 --> 08:43.521
It was my fault.

08:43.521 --> 08:45.611
I'm sorry about that.

08:45.611 --> 08:48.451
No, I've said too much too.

08:48.451 --> 08:50.111
I'm sorry.

08:50.621 --> 08:55.831
Now that we've made up, how about it, tonight?

08:55.831 --> 08:59.581
Let's go avant-garde, baby!

08:59.581 --> 09:02.001
We'll wake up Masao!

09:02.001 --> 09:05.131
But he said he wanted a younger brother.

09:05.131 --> 09:07.801
Awww.

09:10.151 --> 09:10.641
The Loser's Corner

09:10.641 --> 09:13.301
Let's go wilder next time.
The Loser's Corner

09:13.301 --> 09:13.721
They're hopeless.
Let's go wilder next time.
The Loser's Corner

09:13.721 --> 09:14.561
They're hopeless.
The Loser's Corner

09:14.561 --> 09:16.811
The Loser's Corner
They must be serious, but still...

09:16.811 --> 09:17.351
The Loser's Corner

09:17.351 --> 09:17.781
I have to do something.
The Loser's Corner

09:17.781 --> 09:20.141
I have to do something.

09:22.441 --> 09:23.561
Um...

09:24.231 --> 09:25.531
Nice to meet you.

09:25.531 --> 09:27.491
I'm Shiratori Ryushi.

09:27.491 --> 09:29.491
I just moved here recently.

09:30.281 --> 09:32.821
So, what's your name?

09:34.991 --> 09:35.991
Um...

09:53.681 --> 09:54.601
Magic?

09:55.351 --> 09:57.641
But why?

09:58.351 --> 10:00.231
Wow, amazing!

10:00.231 --> 10:03.061
There's no trick to it, but out comes a flurry of confetti!

10:03.061 --> 10:04.811
I'm so surprised!

10:04.811 --> 10:06.481
That's so good!

10:06.481 --> 10:07.071
I know!

10:07.071 --> 10:09.611
I can't do that at all!

10:09.611 --> 10:10.491
Me neither.

10:10.491 --> 10:11.571
You are the best!

10:13.741 --> 10:15.991
Come on, you need to praise her too.

10:16.831 --> 10:19.751
She showed us magic the last time too.

10:19.751 --> 10:24.131
We were in a state of shock then too, just like you are now.

10:24.131 --> 10:27.251
Anyone would get happy and open their heart when they hear praise.

10:27.251 --> 10:29.051
So just praise her.

10:29.051 --> 10:30.301
I see.

10:30.301 --> 10:32.091
That was great!

10:32.091 --> 10:33.761
I want to see more.

10:33.761 --> 10:35.471
Me too! Me too!

10:35.471 --> 10:36.391
What's next?

10:36.391 --> 10:37.811
Hey, hey, hey?

10:48.151 --> 10:50.611
It didn't work again.

10:52.861 --> 10:55.071
She sure is strange.

11:18.181 --> 11:20.141
She's strange, but...

11:20.721 --> 11:24.101
I'm sure she's not a bad girl.

11:50.251 --> 11:52.301
Is that Umeboshi senbei?
TL Note: Senbei is a large, round cracker made out of rice, usually flavored with soy sauce.

11:52.301 --> 11:54.551
TL Note: Senbei is a large, round cracker made out of rice, usually flavored with soy sauce.
So you love umeboshi?

11:54.551 --> 11:56.091
Isn't umeboshi great?

11:56.091 --> 11:58.511
Umeboshi is the best when you feel tired!

12:03.181 --> 12:04.601
Um...

12:04.601 --> 12:06.441
It's a beautiful day today.

12:07.771 --> 12:08.981
Well...

12:08.981 --> 12:11.321
I hope it's beautiful again tomorrow.

12:12.651 --> 12:14.361
I hope it's beautiful...

12:15.151 --> 12:16.241
...the day after tomorrow...

12:18.361 --> 12:20.621
What am I talking about?

12:21.241 --> 12:24.501
Anyway, I need her at least to say a word.

12:26.291 --> 12:28.081
You love to read?

12:28.081 --> 12:30.711
Hey, I'm writing a children's book right now.

12:31.041 --> 12:34.761
Would you read it and tell me what you think when I'm done?

12:36.131 --> 12:37.381
A deck of cards?

13:03.201 --> 13:05.951
Hey, how did you do that?

13:10.121 --> 13:12.921
I can't blame Momono-san and the others, either.

13:13.671 --> 13:14.461
But...

13:17.551 --> 13:19.591
Really, how did she do that?

13:28.681 --> 13:31.731
This is a bit too tough.

13:31.731 --> 13:33.021
Maybe this...

13:37.821 --> 13:39.781
Dang, this time...

13:45.741 --> 13:47.451
Why can't I do it?

13:56.211 --> 13:58.301
You will show it to me?

13:59.591 --> 14:01.091
Thank you.

14:01.091 --> 14:02.471
So...

14:02.471 --> 14:03.511
...like this?

14:05.801 --> 14:07.221
I see!

14:07.221 --> 14:08.521
Makes sense.

14:08.521 --> 14:11.351
Here...

14:11.351 --> 14:12.691
Like this?

14:12.691 --> 14:13.731
This is it.

14:16.321 --> 14:18.691
Hey, do more.

14:19.071 --> 14:20.951
A mouse goes squeak! Squeak!

14:20.951 --> 14:21.611
More...

14:21.611 --> 14:22.571
The strong one doesn't win.
More...

14:22.571 --> 14:23.741
The strong one doesn't win.
A cow goes moo! Moo!

14:23.741 --> 14:25.201
A cow goes moo! Moo!
The one who won is the strong one.

14:25.201 --> 14:26.081
The one who won is the strong one.

14:26.081 --> 14:28.621
Your last one was a good punch.

14:28.621 --> 14:31.211
But the match hasn't ended yet!

14:32.791 --> 14:34.961
I've cried enough, so I'm ready!

14:34.961 --> 14:37.041
Let's go for the second round!

14:39.341 --> 14:40.171
Oh?

14:40.171 --> 14:41.091
Where is She?

14:42.091 --> 14:43.051
Oh?

14:43.471 --> 14:44.931
Oh?

14:52.181 --> 14:53.101
Ready?

15:05.991 --> 15:07.531
So far so good.

15:08.371 --> 15:09.831
But here comes the tough part.

15:25.591 --> 15:28.141
I'm such a klutz.

15:28.141 --> 15:30.311
I can't believe it.

15:30.311 --> 15:31.681
So close...

15:33.641 --> 15:36.191
You were so close.

15:42.781 --> 15:44.191
Yeah!

15:44.191 --> 15:46.361
You finally talked!

15:46.361 --> 15:47.451
I'm so glad.

15:47.451 --> 15:49.991
I'd like to talk like this more often.

15:50.451 --> 15:53.411
We all want to be friends with you.

15:53.411 --> 15:54.331
So...

16:02.671 --> 16:03.591
...maybe.

16:05.051 --> 16:10.101
It'd be boring talking to me, maybe...

16:11.261 --> 16:15.601
I don't have anything fun to say,

16:15.601 --> 16:17.481
I can't read the atmosphere,

16:17.481 --> 16:20.151
I can't be useful to anyone.

16:21.191 --> 16:24.901
So I'm sure it'd be boring to be friends with me.

16:25.861 --> 16:28.161
You don't have to worry about that.

16:28.611 --> 16:34.371
We don't become friends just because we're useful or fun.

16:34.371 --> 16:35.791
We may be boring.

16:35.791 --> 16:37.751
Or maybe cause a lot of trouble.

16:37.751 --> 16:40.211
Or cause a lot of misfortune.

16:40.541 --> 16:42.211
But we still want to be together.

16:42.211 --> 16:43.841
That's what...

16:45.091 --> 16:46.921
...we call being friends.

16:48.591 --> 16:52.971
Besides, I still don't know anything about you.

16:53.431 --> 16:57.271
I can't like or hate you unless I get to know you.

16:57.271 --> 16:58.981
Of course, we can't become friends either.

16:59.691 --> 17:01.021
Friends...

17:04.271 --> 17:06.361
Or so I think.

17:06.361 --> 17:09.151
Is that not good enough?

17:10.411 --> 17:11.531
I...

17:13.991 --> 17:18.371
When you called me a friend earlier,

17:19.001 --> 17:22.671
it made me feel fuzzy... maybe.

17:22.671 --> 17:23.631
Fuzzy?

17:24.291 --> 17:27.631
I'm gloomy,

17:28.381 --> 17:30.881
can't say anything fun,

17:32.431 --> 17:36.221
and useless.

17:37.771 --> 17:43.021
Would you still be my friend?

17:44.191 --> 17:45.691
Of course!

17:45.691 --> 17:47.031
It'd be my pleasure.

17:55.911 --> 17:59.251
There is one thing I know about you.

17:59.251 --> 18:00.911
You're good at magic.

18:02.121 --> 18:04.921
I'm Natsume.

18:05.841 --> 18:07.421
My name...

18:08.051 --> 18:09.421
Konno Natsume              ...maybe

18:09.421 --> 18:12.221
Konno Natsume... maybe...
Konno Natsume              ...maybe

18:12.631 --> 18:13.391
Maybe?

18:13.391 --> 18:15.221
Hey!

18:15.641 --> 18:18.221
We came up with a new plan!

18:18.221 --> 18:22.101
I guarantee it will open her heart!

18:23.231 --> 18:24.981
Everyone...

18:27.731 --> 18:29.651
Why only with Shiratori-kun?!

18:29.651 --> 18:31.701
Shiratori-san, that's not fair!

18:31.701 --> 18:33.161
How could you?!

18:33.161 --> 18:35.121
How'd you do it, Onii-chan?

18:35.781 --> 18:36.781
Yay...

18:36.781 --> 18:39.831
Calm down, everyone.

18:40.291 --> 18:43.671
I'm sure you can be friends with everyone,

18:43.671 --> 18:45.381
although it might take some time.

18:50.921 --> 18:54.381
The fun time with it ended abruptly.

18:55.221 --> 19:00.181
It disappeared at the end of summer.

19:00.181 --> 19:02.141
The man thought...

19:02.141 --> 19:04.061
...that farewells are always harsh.

19:04.061 --> 19:06.151
They're always harsh and sad.

19:06.651 --> 19:10.781
If he never encountered anyone, then he wouldn't suffer so much.

19:11.781 --> 19:14.531
If he hadn't met her...

19:16.111 --> 19:20.581
If it makes him so sad, why should he want to meet anyone?

19:21.621 --> 19:22.041
So...

19:24.461 --> 19:25.331
So...

19:35.631 --> 19:36.641
But...

19:37.591 --> 19:41.181
...if they hadn't met, he would never have had such happy times.

19:47.401 --> 19:50.821
Eventually, the man started going into town again.

19:53.321 --> 19:56.031
He learned not to be afraid of farewells, to meet people,

19:56.661 --> 19:59.321
to not be afraid of misunderstandings, and to get to know others.

20:02.451 --> 20:06.461
There may be harsh farewells like the harshness of winter,

20:08.671 --> 20:11.341
but one day he can meet someone again.

20:12.501 --> 20:14.841
Someday, he can meet a person...

20:17.181 --> 20:19.511
...as warm as the spring sunlight.

20:22.511 --> 20:26.021
Narutakisou

20:31.651 --> 20:34.651
Oh, I fell asleep again.

20:56.421 --> 20:57.471
I did it!

20:59.471 --> 21:00.681
Kozue-chan!

21:01.591 --> 21:03.561
That's amazing, Shiratori-san!

21:03.561 --> 21:06.221
I didn't know you had such talent.

21:07.431 --> 21:08.941
I just learned it.

21:08.941 --> 21:10.061
Just learned it?

21:10.401 --> 21:12.811
Yup, from an important friend.

21:12.811 --> 21:14.651
I see.

21:14.651 --> 21:20.611
Oh, I haven't heard all of the story you were writing.

21:20.611 --> 21:23.411
Will you still tell me the rest?

21:23.701 --> 21:24.871
Yeah.

21:24.871 --> 21:26.701
But let me tell you this first.

21:26.701 --> 21:30.041
It has a happy end, so don't worry and listen to it all the way to the end.

21:30.331 --> 21:30.961
Yes!

21:30.961 --> 21:32.171
I can't wait!

21:32.171 --> 21:33.211
What?

21:33.211 --> 21:34.591
What story?

21:34.591 --> 21:38.301
Shiratori-san, only to Kozue-chan?

21:38.301 --> 21:40.091
I want to hear it!

21:40.091 --> 21:41.301
Me too.

21:41.301 --> 21:43.261
Start from the beginning.

21:43.261 --> 21:44.931
Okay, fine.

21:44.931 --> 21:46.511
Then from the beginning...

21:47.681 --> 21:51.521
It's a story about something that happened to a man a long, long time ago.

21:59.441 --> 22:05.951
One day, I drew a picture all over a canvas,
itsu no hika canvas ni e ippai

22:06.031 --> 22:11.751
a picture of 7-colored dreams.
nanairo no yume egaita

22:13.171 --> 22:19.631
When I noticed, I was a bit more grown up.
ki ga tsukeba sukoshi otona ni natte

22:19.881 --> 22:24.931
What have I found?
nani wo mitsuketandarou

22:26.891 --> 22:33.641
In this aimless daily life,
yuka ate no nai mainichi no nakade

22:33.891 --> 22:39.571
I found something that's most important.
ichiban taisetsuna koto ni kizuita

22:40.571 --> 22:46.411
Yes, it's always all right,
donna tokidemo sousa daijoubu

22:46.411 --> 22:48.661
because you are here.
kimi ga irukara

22:48.871 --> 22:55.041
Holding these unforgettable thoughts,
wasurenai kono omoi dakishimete

22:55.541 --> 23:01.381
I will start walking the path of the halted fantasy again,
mouichido togireta yume no fantasy

23:01.381 --> 23:06.011
at my own speed.
aruitemiyou boku no speed de

23:22.021 --> 23:22.601
